WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.291
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:04.291 --> 00:00:05.374
- Give it up!

00:00:08.509 --> 00:00:09.749
Have a seat.

00:00:09.749 --> 00:00:13.749
(audience yelling and clapping)

00:00:20.328 --> 00:00:25.029
Give it up, give it up.

00:00:25.029 --> 00:00:29.376
This is exciting today, in five seasons,

00:00:29.376 --> 00:00:30.623
this has never happened.

00:00:30.623 --> 00:00:33.600
We have had rowdy audiences,
but in five seasons,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.244
you win.
- [Olivia] Oh man.

00:00:35.244 --> 00:00:36.690
- That is, you all get an award.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:37.830
That was insane.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.565
Congratulations on all the Grammy noms.

00:00:39.565 --> 00:00:41.787
- Oh, thank you, thank you.

00:00:41.787 --> 00:00:42.997
(audience cheering)

00:00:42.997 --> 00:00:44.925
It's gonna keep happening.

00:00:44.925 --> 00:00:46.437
- Well, congrats on
yours too, it's amazing.

00:00:46.437 --> 00:00:49.830
- I was telling, I was
telling her backstage,

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:52.535
I was telling her
backstage, the win for me

00:00:52.535 --> 00:00:54.780
is literally who I'm nominated with.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:55.830
Like that's the win for me.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.750
I was telling her, like I always see like

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.640
who's in the same category,
and I'm like (gasps).

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:01.350
And everybody is so good.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:02.198
- Yeah.

00:01:02.198 --> 00:01:03.031
- In the category we're both in,

00:01:03.031 --> 00:01:05.051
I was like oh my god, so
that's the win for me.

00:01:05.051 --> 00:01:05.884
- Yeah, it's so...

00:01:05.884 --> 00:01:06.717
- To be like amongst your peers

00:01:06.717 --> 00:01:07.550
that you're just like oh my god.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:08.383
- [Olivia] Yeah.

00:01:08.383 --> 00:01:09.216
- Like those are people
I would collaborate with,

00:01:09.216 --> 00:01:11.313
I listen to, I love, like
that's the win for me.

00:01:11.313 --> 00:01:12.750
- It's so nice to be like included

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.010
in such a wonderful group of people.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:15.780
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.790
What, I don't know, what's
your most meaningful nom?

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.050
Was it your first one?

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:20.601
That was for "Sour", that record.

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:22.500
- Yeah, yeah, I got nominated
for "Sour", which was so cool.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.440
This year I actually got
nominated for best rock song

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:26.643
for "Ballad of a Homeschooled Girl".

00:01:26.643 --> 00:01:29.393
(audience cheering)

00:01:29.393 --> 00:01:30.811
Which is so cool.

00:01:30.811 --> 00:01:31.877
- That's an amazing thing.

00:01:31.877 --> 00:01:35.970
I hear on your, so on tour you saw me,

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:36.803
or they're right here.

00:01:36.803 --> 00:01:38.100
They're in-ears, we call them in-ears,

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.450
but you can decorate them.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.250
And I go gold sparkly seventies.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.083
- [Olivia] Cute.

00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:43.500
- But you have photos on yours.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:44.380
I didn't know you could do photos.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:46.073
- Yeah, you can put photos.

00:01:46.073 --> 00:01:46.906
- No one told me this.

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.570
- Yeah, you put photos of your
kids, put photos of anyone.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.334
Those are mine.

00:01:50.334 --> 00:01:51.574
- [Kelly] Edward Cullen.

00:01:51.574 --> 00:01:53.250
- That's my, that's my baby.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:54.507
Like, that's my thing.

00:01:54.507 --> 00:01:55.650
- I'm a "Twilight" nerd.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:57.560
- That's Edward Cullen on my in-ears.

00:01:58.443 --> 00:01:59.830
(audience cheering)

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:00.690
He is my...

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:02.554
- The purple lavender,
I like it too, yeah.

00:02:02.554 --> 00:02:03.420
- Yeah, he's my guiding light on tour.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:04.538
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:04.538 --> 00:02:05.942
- I have to have my lucky charm.

00:02:05.942 --> 00:02:07.440
Yeah, love him.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.030
- What's on your in-ears now?

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.620
- My in-ears now for this Guts tour,

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.390
I'm gonna get a new face every tour,

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:14.280
so taking suggestions for the next one.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:15.330
Maybe I'll put you on my next one.

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:18.750
- Okay, aim for like something random.

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:21.040
Like Betty White, like just
something random, right?

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.588
- Yeah, but this year it's um.

00:02:22.588 --> 00:02:23.421
- It makes you happy.

00:02:23.421 --> 00:02:24.254
- Totally.

00:02:24.254 --> 00:02:25.087
- Oh, it's Kim Cattrall.

00:02:25.087 --> 00:02:26.697
- Yeah, it's Kim Cattrall.

00:02:26.697 --> 00:02:28.559
(audience cheering)

00:02:28.559 --> 00:02:29.392
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:02:29.392 --> 00:02:30.870
- It's Kim Cattrall
from "Sex in the City",

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:31.860
Samantha from "Sex in the City".

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:34.200
She's my favorite, and she's
like drinking a little martini,

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.040
and I thought it was great.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:35.873
- Why not.

00:02:35.873 --> 00:02:37.134
- [Olivia] Why not.

00:02:37.134 --> 00:02:37.967
- You know what, that's says celebrate,

00:02:37.967 --> 00:02:38.910
every time you put your
in-ears in, I like it.

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:39.842
- Yeah, uh huh.

00:02:39.842 --> 00:02:40.675
- I think I did know you could do photos.

00:02:40.675 --> 00:02:41.580
Do you have Rue?

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:42.990
Do you have Rue on yours?

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:43.860
Oh, okay, her dog.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:45.578
I was like maybe I have seen photos.

00:02:45.578 --> 00:02:46.411
- [Olivia] Oh cute.

00:02:46.411 --> 00:02:48.030
- [Kelly] I know, I need to be cooler.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:49.111
I'm gonna aim higher.

00:02:49.111 --> 00:02:49.944
- [Olivia] Next time.
- Okay.

00:02:49.944 --> 00:02:52.860
In honor of her album, "Guts,
we are hosting a Gutsy Hour.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:56.130
Everyone in the audience has
taken a very gutsy chance

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:59.700
and many have Olivia to thank
for inspiring them to do so.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.140
It's weird 'cause you don't
think you're gonna have

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:04.410
that kind of impact on
someone, but it really does.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:05.940
Music is so magical like that

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:07.290
So, why "Guts"?

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:08.610
Why that for your title?

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.440
- Yeah, I just always loved the word.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.810
I think it has so many
interesting meanings.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:14.490
It means bravery.

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:16.140
Spilling your guts means
like telling everyone

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:17.850
your dirty little
secrets, which I feel like

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:19.170
is just what I do in my song.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:20.820
- Yeah, amen.

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:22.800
- Yeah, so it's just a
really powerful word.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.540
And I like a four letter word, you know.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.190
- [Kelly] Me too, yeah.

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:27.900
- Gotta love a four letter
word every now and then.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.640
So yeah, it just became the title.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:30.600
- I love that.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.070
I love all the separate kind of ways

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:32.903
you can take it as well.

00:03:32.903 --> 00:03:33.960
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:35.640
Will you tell us about some lyrics.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:36.480
We pulled some.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.560
- Oh yeah, sure.
- [Kelly] Do you mind?

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.720
Okay, because there's so many good ones.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.287
In "Lacy", Olivia writes,

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:44.107
"And I despise my jealous
eyes and how hard"

00:03:44.107 --> 00:03:45.247
"they fell for you."

00:03:45.247 --> 00:03:46.957
"Yeah, I despise my rotten mind"

00:03:46.957 --> 00:03:48.300
"and how much it worships you."

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.057
I mean, that last line.

00:03:51.057 --> 00:03:53.730
(audience cheering)

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:55.828
I despise my rotten mind.

00:03:55.828 --> 00:03:57.166
- [Olivia] Oh man.

00:03:57.166 --> 00:03:58.650
- And how much it worships
you, I'm like that,

00:03:58.650 --> 00:03:59.640
who has not felt?

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:03.300
You have a very poetic
way, kind of like Alanis,

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.400
like you have a poetic way
of like wording things,

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.720
but they're so relatable.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:07.930
- Thanks.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:08.763
- [Kelly] But it's so poetic.

00:04:08.763 --> 00:04:11.076
- Wow, yeah, it's very
emo of me writing that.

00:04:11.076 --> 00:04:11.909
- [Kelly] What were you thinking there?

00:04:11.909 --> 00:04:12.890
- Yeah.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:13.727
- I like emo, that's all right.

00:04:13.727 --> 00:04:15.297
- Me too, me too.

00:04:15.297 --> 00:04:17.940
- Um, I took a poetry
class actually at USC

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:18.840
this year, last year?

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:22.680
And I wrote a poem called "Lacy"
for one of the assignments.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:23.513
And I really liked it, and I'm like

00:04:23.513 --> 00:04:24.360
I'm gonna turn it into a song.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.130
So that's sort of where
that one came from.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:27.210
- When do you have time to go to college?

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:29.430
- I know, I know.

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:30.300
- [Kelly] Back that train up.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:31.620
- I just took one class.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:32.940
I was going to the studio some days,

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:33.960
and then I'd go to college

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.880
and like it was fun, it was fun, yeah.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:36.713
- That is so cool.

00:04:36.713 --> 00:04:37.546
I love that you did that.

00:04:37.546 --> 00:04:39.390
It's always cool to
like progress and grow.

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:42.072
- Yeah, I always wanna
stay curious, you know.

00:04:42.072 --> 00:04:44.190
- You've got a great song
out of it, damn, all right.

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:47.767
So next, in "All American
Bitch", Olivia says,

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:49.375
"I am". (audience cheering)

00:04:49.375 --> 00:04:50.208
They like it.

00:04:50.208 --> 00:04:51.041
"I am light as a feather."

00:04:51.041 --> 00:04:52.087
"I'm as stiff as a board."

00:04:52.087 --> 00:04:54.480
"I pay attention to things
that most people ignore."

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.060
So first of all, what do
you know about that game?

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:58.975
That's a game I played when I was a kid.

00:04:58.975 --> 00:05:00.112
- Yeah.

00:05:00.112 --> 00:05:00.945
- [Kelly] Did you all do that?

00:05:00.945 --> 00:05:01.778
Light as a feather, stiff as a board?

00:05:01.778 --> 00:05:02.611
- Have you ever done it?

00:05:02.611 --> 00:05:03.444
Okay, did it work?

00:05:03.444 --> 00:05:04.277
- Well, here's the thing.

00:05:04.277 --> 00:05:07.110
There's like 15 of you around
a body with your fingers.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.730
And you're all doing it at the same time.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:10.509
That's what we did, so of
course we're all gonna lift 'em.

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:12.393
These are powerful fingers.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.120
Like it was all of us,
and we're all like tiny

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:16.234
at the time we were playing it, yeah.

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:17.067
- That's true, that's true.

00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:17.910
Well, my mom used to tell me

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:19.350
about doing that at sleepovers.

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:20.193
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:20.193 --> 00:05:21.026
- So that's how I knew
the light as a feather,

00:05:21.026 --> 00:05:21.859
stiff as a board thing.

00:05:21.859 --> 00:05:22.692
- [Kelly] That's what I did, yeah.

00:05:22.692 --> 00:05:23.525
- And I was always fascinated by it.

00:05:23.525 --> 00:05:24.358
I'm like, that seems impossible.

00:05:24.358 --> 00:05:26.460
Like I need some physicist
to like explain it to me.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:27.293
- Yeah.

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:30.480
I think it's just literally
we want it to be magical.

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:31.319
- [Olivia] Yeah.

00:05:31.319 --> 00:05:32.370
- But really, it's all
of us just underneath.

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:33.270
- You're just forcing it really hard.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.455
- Yeah lifting the person up.
- Yeah.

00:05:35.455 --> 00:05:36.443
- We're like how is this happening?

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:38.460
- Yeah, but I always thought it was

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:39.960
a really interesting phrase,

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:40.793
and so I've been trying to get it

00:05:40.793 --> 00:05:42.120
into a song for a long time.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:44.370
So I thought it was an
interesting way to describe,

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:46.230
like it seems kind of
impossible, light as a feather,

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:48.150
stiff as a board, so I thought
it was a good way to describe

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:50.010
kind of the impossible standards

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:51.210
that are set for us as women.

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:52.043
So it's just kind of.

00:05:52.043 --> 00:05:53.239
- [Kelly] Yeah, I love it.

00:05:53.239 --> 00:05:54.465
- It wrote itself, yeah.

00:05:54.465 --> 00:05:55.298
(audience cheering)

00:05:55.298 --> 00:05:56.910
- I love that you take something
that everybody knows too

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:58.406
and you twist it into something.

00:05:58.406 --> 00:05:59.490
That's very smart.

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:01.350
Well, we have an audience full of people

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:04.230
who have been inspired by Olivia
to take some gutsy chances.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.700
But before we hear them,

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:07.230
I feel like we should share ours.

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:09.750
I'll share, I was kind of
sharing a little bit of mine

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:13.320
in the break, but I get tattoos.

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:15.900
Well, not all of them, but a lot of them

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.580
are when not great things happen.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:21.870
And I do it because I like
the reminder that I made it,

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:25.920
and like, it sometimes things
seem so big in your world

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:28.740
at that moment and you feel
like you're not gonna make it.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.330
And then you do, and so usually

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:31.780
that's when I get the tattoo.

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:35.030
One of my favorites is
on my middle finger.

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:37.290
Yeah, and it says DC.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:38.820
And it's 'cause somebody made me feel,

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:40.710
and I don't know, I hope
you never experience this

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:43.080
or haven't, but 'cause I
do think we've progressed

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:43.920
a little in this industry.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:47.010
But, yeah, people can be very mean.

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:49.500
I mean, they can be just vicious.

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:51.450
And it's, you know, if
you're not successful

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:53.070
how they want you to be
or doing what you want,

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:55.080
and it's usually their shortcomings.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:55.913
- [Olivia] Sure.

00:06:55.913 --> 00:06:57.360
- And I mean, someone was so vicious.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:00.180
And I was so tired of sitting in a room

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:01.890
where men just made me feel like (beep).

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.450
And then I was like, you know what?

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:07.710
Nope, I actually had
the guts to finally say,

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:09.740
and I was in my twenties,
you know, I started at 19.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.210
So I was, it took a
minute, but I finally said

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:14.760
like you know what, I was like actually,

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.740
I think this is about you
and I think this is about.

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:19.620
And I just totally said
everything I've ever wanted to say

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:21.450
in that moment, so that's
one of my favorite tattoos.

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:23.300
- Wow, that's beautiful.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:24.318
(audience cheering)

00:07:24.318 --> 00:07:25.750
- Yeah, I hope you don't go through that.

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:27.320
But, what's one of yours?

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:29.010
- Oh my gosh, my gutsy story?

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:31.140
After that beautiful story,
mine's gonna sound so silly.

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:32.100
I don't know.

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:32.933
- No it won't, make it lighter.

00:07:32.933 --> 00:07:33.766
- [Olivia] Okay, okay.

00:07:33.766 --> 00:07:35.100
- I was a little heavy for day time.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:36.230
(Olivia laughing)

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:37.500
- Okay, I'll make it day time.

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:40.770
I was thinking coming up
here, 'cause we're at 30 Rock,

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:41.603
we're in New York.

00:07:41.603 --> 00:07:42.436
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:42.436 --> 00:07:43.860
- The second time I ever
performed in my career

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:46.244
was on SNL, and I was 18-years-old.

00:07:46.244 --> 00:07:47.649
(audience cheering)

00:07:47.649 --> 00:07:48.482
- Wow.

00:07:48.482 --> 00:07:49.770
- And I was so, which is incredible.

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:52.470
I mean, what an honor,
but I was terrified.

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:53.490
- Yes, and it's so late.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:54.627
- [Olivia] It's so late, yes.

00:07:54.627 --> 00:07:55.860
- [Kelly] For a vocalist.

00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:56.970
- Yes, and it's so live.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:58.950
- [Kelly] Uh huh, yeah.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:07:59.820
